/-!
# The kernel of the generic-point map and the local rings of a normal integral scheme

Let `X` be an integral scheme with function field `K = κ(η)` at its generic point `η`. For every
point `x` of `X` the inclusion of the generic point factors through the spectrum of the local
ring `𝒪_{X,x}`, so the continuous homomorphism `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)` factors as

```
π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x}) → π₁(X),
```

and therefore the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` is contained in the kernel of
`π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`. Consequently the smallest closed normal subgroup of `π₁(Spec K)`
containing all of these kernels is contained in the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`.

When `X` is moreover normal, the local exact sequence of Stacks Tag 0BSM identifies each of those
kernels with the smallest closed normal subgroup of `π₁(Spec K)` containing the image of
`π₁(Spec K_x^sh)`, where `K_x^sh` is the fraction field of a strict henselization of `𝒪_{X,x}`.
So the subgroup appearing above is the third of the three subgroups of Stacks Tag 0BTD, and the
kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)` is the first; one of the things proved here is the inclusion
`(3) ⊆ (1)`. The second subgroup of the tag, generated by the inertia groups on the
normalization of `X` in `K^sep`, is also constructed here, and the kernel of
`π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)` is shown to be contained in it: the inclusion `(1) ⊆ (2)`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkToGenericResidueField` — the canonical ring map `𝒪_{X,x} → κ(η)` from
  the local ring at a point of an irreducible scheme to the residue field at the generic point,
  together with the algebra structure and (for `X` integral) the fraction-field property it
  carries.

## Main results

* `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.isLeast_normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure` — for a family of
  subgroups `Hᵢ` of a topological group, `(normalClosure (⋃ i, Hᵢ)).topologicalClosure` is the
  smallest closed normal subgroup containing every `Hᵢ`;
  `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff` is the membership
  criterion this yields, and
  `Stacks.FundamentalGroup.normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_eq` says that replacing each
  member of the family by the closed normal subgroup it generates does not change the result.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_le_ker` — the kernel of
  `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` is contained in the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.normalClosure_iUnion_ker_topologicalClosure_le_ker` — the inclusion
  `(3) ⊆ (1)` of Stacks Tag 0BTD, with subgroup `(3)` written as the smallest closed normal
  subgroup containing all the kernels above.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_eq_normalClosure_topologicalClosure` —
  each of those kernels is the smallest closed normal subgroup containing the image of
  `π₁(Spec K_x^sh)`, which is how the source writes the generators of subgroup `(3)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.normalClosure_range_topologicalClosure_le_ker` — the same inclusion with
  subgroup `(3)` written through its own generators, one point of `X` at a time: the smallest
  closed normal subgroup of `π₁(Spec K)` containing the image of `Gal(K^sep/K_x^sh)` is
  contained in the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.comap_normalClosure_iUnion_ker_le_ker_galoisToFundamentalGroup` — the same
  inclusion read inside `Gal(K^sep/K)` through the identification of Stacks Tag 0BNE.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup` — subgroup `(2)` of Stacks Tag 0BTD, the
  smallest closed normal subgroup of `Gal(K^sep/K)` containing the inertia group `I_y` at every
  point `y` of the normalization `X^sep` of `X` in `K^sep`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFinite_etale_fromNormalization_of_inertiaGenerators_subset` — if every
  `I_y` restricts to the identity on a finite Galois subextension `F` of `K^sep/K`, then `X` is
  unramified in `F`; this is the second paragraph of the source's proof, through Stacks Tags
  0BSX and 0BTF.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_galoisToFundamentalGroup_le_inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup` — the reverse
  inclusion `(1) ⊆ (2)` of Stacks Tag 0BTD.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkKerClosedNormalSubgroup` — subgroup `(3)` of Stacks Tag 0BTD read
  inside `Gal(K^sep/K)`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup_le_stalkKerClosedNormalSubgroup` — the remaining
  inclusion `(2) ⊆ (3)`, which closes the cycle `(3) ⊆ (1) ⊆ (2) ⊆ (3)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_galoisToFundamentalGroup_eq_inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup_and_stalkKer` —
  the resulting **equality of the three subgroups of Stacks Tag 0BTD**.

## Implementation notes

Subgroup `(1)` of the source is the kernel of the surjection `Gal(K^sep/K) → π₁(X)`, which under
the identification `Gal(K^sep/K) = π₁(Spec K)` of Stacks Tag 0BNE
(`AlgebraicGeometry.galoisEquivEtaleFundamentalGroup`) is the kernel of the homomorphism induced
by `X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X)`. That is the form used here; the final result
transports it to `Gal(K^sep/K)` along that identification, where the induced homomorphism is
`AlgebraicGeometry.galoisToFundamentalGroup`. Surjectivity is Stacks Tag 0BQM, which is not used:
only the kernel matters below. In particular nothing here needs `X` to be Noetherian — the
description of subgroup `(1)` as the subgroup fixing the maximal unramified subextension does,
through Stacks Tag 03VG, but that description is not used.

Subgroup `(3)` is written as the smallest closed normal subgroup containing the kernels of
`π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` rather than the images of the `π₁(Spec K_x^sh)`. The two agree:
`AlgebraicGeometry.ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_eq_normalClosure_topologicalClosure`
identifies each kernel with the closed normal subgroup generated by the corresponding image, and
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_eq` says that passing from the
images to the subgroups they generate leaves the closed normal subgroup generated by the whole
family unchanged. The kernels are preferred in the statement because they are subgroups of
`π₁(Spec K, p)` for one fixed base point `p`, whereas the image of `π₁(Spec K_x^sh)` is a
subgroup of `π₁(Spec K, q.map f)` for a base point `q` of `Spec K_x^sh`, which varies with `x`.

Subgroup `(2)` of the source — the smallest closed normal subgroup containing the inertia groups
`I_y` for `y` a point of the normalization `X^sep` of `X` in `K^sep` — is
`AlgebraicGeometry.inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup`. The normalization `X^sep` is affine over `X`,
so its points over a nonempty affine open `U` of `X` are the primes of the integral closure of
`Γ(X, U)` in `K^sep`, and the inertia group at such a point is the ring-theoretic
`Ideal.inertia` there; that is how the index set `y ∈ X^sep` is presented, exactly as the
inertia condition of Stacks Tag 0BTF is presented in
`AlgebraicGeometry.normalization_unramified_iff_trivialInertia`.

The inclusion `(2) ⊆ (3)` is proved in the last section. The source gets it from the conjugacy
of `I_y` with `Gal(K^sep/K_x^sh)` for `y` over `x` (Stacks Tag 0BSW), which rests on the
identification `K_x^sh = (K^sep)^{I_y}`; here it comes from the same identification in the form
`Stacks.RamificationTheory.comap_ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_eq_normalClosure_inertia`, after
`IsIntegralClosure.exists_isMaximal_inertia_eq_of_isLocalization` has moved the inertia group at
a prime of the integral closure of `Γ(X, U)` to one at a maximal ideal of the integral closure of
`𝒪_{X,x}`. Together with the two inclusions above this gives the cycle `(3) ⊆ (1) ⊆ (2) ⊆ (3)`,
so the three subgroups of the source are equal.

The ring map `𝒪_{X,x} → κ(η)` is the specialization map `𝒪_{X,x} → 𝒪_{X,η}` of Mathlib followed
by the residue map at `η`, which for an integral scheme is an isomorphism onto the function field;
this is what makes `κ(η)` a fraction field of `𝒪_{X,x}`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BTD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BTD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BSM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BSM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BNE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BNE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BND](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BND)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace Stacks.FundamentalGroup

/-! ### The smallest closed normal subgroup containing a family of subgroups -/

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G] [IsTopologicalGroup G]

/-- A set is contained in the closed normal subgroup it generates. -/
theorem subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure (S : Set G) :
    S ⊆ ((Subgroup.normalClosure S).topologicalClosure : Set G) :=
  Set.Subset.trans Subgroup.subset_normalClosure
    (Subgroup.le_topologicalClosure (Subgroup.normalClosure S))

/-- The closed normal subgroup generated by a set is contained in every closed normal subgroup
containing that set. -/
theorem normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le {S : Set G} {N : Subgroup G} [N.Normal]
    (hN : IsClosed (N : Set G)) (hS : S ⊆ (N : Set G)) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure S).topologicalClosure ≤ N :=
  Subgroup.topologicalClosure_minimal _ (Subgroup.normalClosure_le_normal hS) hN

/-- A closed normal subgroup contains the closed normal subgroup generated by a set exactly when
it contains the set. -/
theorem normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le_iff {S : Set G} {N : Subgroup G} [N.Normal]
    (hN : IsClosed (N : Set G)) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure S).topologicalClosure ≤ N ↔ S ⊆ (N : Set G) :=
  ⟨fun h => Set.Subset.trans (subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure S) h,
    normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le hN⟩

/-- The closed normal subgroup generated by a set is the smallest closed normal subgroup
containing it. -/
theorem isLeast_normalClosure_topologicalClosure (S : Set G) :
    IsLeast {N : Subgroup G | N.Normal ∧ IsClosed (N : Set G) ∧ S ⊆ (N : Set G)}
      (Subgroup.normalClosure S).topologicalClosure :=
  ⟨⟨Subgroup.is_normal_topologicalClosure _, Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _,
      subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure S⟩,
    fun _ hN => have := hN.1; normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le hN.2.1 hN.2.2⟩

variable {ι : Sort*}

/-- Each member of a family of subgroups is contained in the closed normal subgroup generated by
the family. -/
theorem le_normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure (H : ι → Subgroup G) (i : ι) :
    H i ≤ (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ j, (H j : Set G))).topologicalClosure := fun _ hg =>
  subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure _ (Set.mem_iUnion_of_mem i hg)

/-- A closed normal subgroup contains the closed normal subgroup generated by a family of
subgroups exactly when it contains every member of the family. -/
theorem normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff (H : ι → Subgroup G) {N : Subgroup G}
    [N.Normal] (hN : IsClosed (N : Set G)) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ j, (H j : Set G))).topologicalClosure ≤ N ↔ ∀ i, H i ≤ N := by
  rw [normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le_iff hN, Set.iUnion_subset_iff]
  rfl

/-- The closed normal subgroup generated by a family of subgroups is the smallest closed normal
subgroup containing every member of the family. -/
theorem isLeast_normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure (H : ι → Subgroup G) :
    IsLeast {N : Subgroup G | N.Normal ∧ IsClosed (N : Set G) ∧ ∀ i, H i ≤ N}
      (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ j, (H j : Set G))).topologicalClosure := by
  refine ⟨⟨Subgroup.is_normal_topologicalClosure _, Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _,
    le_normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure H⟩, fun N hN => ?_⟩
  have := hN.1
  exact (normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff H hN.2.1).mpr hN.2.2

/-- An open subgroup of a topological group is closed, so it contains the closed normal subgroup
generated by a family of subgroups exactly when it contains every member of the family. -/
theorem normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff_of_isOpen (H : ι → Subgroup G)
    {U : Subgroup G} [U.Normal] (hU : IsOpen (U : Set G)) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ j, (H j : Set G))).topologicalClosure ≤ U ↔ ∀ i, H i ≤ U :=
  normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff H (Subgroup.isClosed_of_isOpen U hU)

/-- Replacing each member of a family of sets by the closed normal subgroup it generates does not
change the closed normal subgroup generated by the whole family. -/
theorem normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_eq {S : ι → Set G} {H : ι → Subgroup G}
    (h : ∀ i, H i = (Subgroup.normalClosure (S i)).topologicalClosure) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ i, (H i : Set G))).topologicalClosure
      = (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ i, S i)).topologicalClosure := by
  have : (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ i, S i)).topologicalClosure.Normal :=
    Subgroup.is_normal_topologicalClosure _
  have : (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ i, (H i : Set G))).topologicalClosure.Normal :=
    Subgroup.is_normal_topologicalClosure _
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · refine (normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff H
      (Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _)).mpr fun i => ?_
    rw [h i]
    exact normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le (Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _)
      (Set.Subset.trans (Set.subset_iUnion S i) (subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure _))
  · refine normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le (Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _) ?_
    refine Set.iUnion_subset fun i => Set.Subset.trans ?_
      (le_normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure H i)
    rw [h i]
    exact subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure _

end Stacks.FundamentalGroup

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-! ### The local rings of an integral scheme and its function field -/

variable (X : Scheme.{u})

/-- The canonical ring map from the local ring of an irreducible scheme at a point to the residue
field at the generic point: specialization to the generic point, followed by the residue map
there. -/
def stalkToGenericResidueField [IrreducibleSpace X] (x : X) :
    X.presheaf.stalk x ⟶ X.residueField (genericPoint X) :=
  X.presheaf.stalkSpecializes ((genericPoint_spec X).specializes (Set.mem_univ x)) ≫
    X.residue (genericPoint X)

/-- The residue field at the generic point of an irreducible scheme is an algebra over every
local ring, through `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkToGenericResidueField`. -/
instance stalkGenericResidueFieldAlgebra [IrreducibleSpace X] (x : X) :
    Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) :=
  (stalkToGenericResidueField X x).hom.toAlgebra

/-- The structure map of `AlgebraicGeometry.stalkGenericResidueFieldAlgebra` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.stalkToGenericResidueField`. -/
theorem ofHom_algebraMap_stalk_genericResidueField [IrreducibleSpace X] (x : X) :
    CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)))
      = stalkToGenericResidueField X x :=
  rfl

/-- **The inclusion of the generic point factors through the spectrum of any local ring.** -/
theorem Spec_map_stalkToGenericResidueField_fromSpecStalk [IrreducibleSpace X] (x : X) :
    Spec.map (stalkToGenericResidueField X x) ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x =
      X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X) := by
  rw [stalkToGenericResidueField, Spec.map_comp, Category.assoc,
    Scheme.SpecMap_stalkSpecializes_fromSpecStalk]
  rfl

/-- **The residue field at the generic point of an integral scheme is a fraction field of every
local ring.** It is the function field up to the residue isomorphism at the generic point, and
the function field is a fraction field of every local ring. -/
@[ega "I 8.2.1"]
instance isFractionRing_stalk_genericResidueField [IsIntegral X] (x : X) :
    IsFractionRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) := by
  have := isIso_residue_genericPoint X
  let e : X.functionField ≃ₐ[X.presheaf.stalk x] X.residueField (genericPoint X) :=
    { (asIso (X.residue (genericPoint X))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv with
      commutes' := fun _ => rfl }
  exact IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_algEquiv _ e

/-! ### The kernels of the maps to the local rings -/

/-- A class killed by a morphism of étale fundamental groups is killed by any morphism it
factors through. -/
private theorem etaleFundamentalGroupMap_comp_eq_one {Y W Z : Scheme.{u}} [ConnectedSpace Y]
    [ConnectedSpace W] [ConnectedSpace Z] (g : Y ⟶ W) (k : W ⟶ Z) (y : GeometricPoint Y)
    (σ : EtaleFundamentalGroup Y y) (hσ : etaleFundamentalGroupMap g y σ = 1) :
    etaleFundamentalGroupMap (g ≫ k) y σ = 1 := by
  cases GeometricPoint.map_map g k y
  have hc := eq_of_heq (etaleFundamentalGroupMap_comp g k y σ)
  rw [← hc, hσ]
  exact map_one _

/-- **The kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` is contained in the kernel of
`π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`.** The inclusion of the generic point factors through the spectrum of the
local ring at `x`, so the second homomorphism factors through the first. -/
theorem ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_le_ker [IsIntegral X] (x : X)
    (p : GeometricPoint (Spec (X.residueField (genericPoint X)))) :
    (etaleFundamentalGroupMap (Spec.map (stalkToGenericResidueField X x)) p).toMonoidHom.ker ≤
      (etaleFundamentalGroupMap (X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X))
        p).toMonoidHom.ker := by
  intro σ hσ
  rw [MonoidHom.mem_ker] at hσ ⊢
  rw [← Spec_map_stalkToGenericResidueField_fromSpecStalk X x]
  exact etaleFundamentalGroupMap_comp_eq_one _ _ p σ hσ

/-- The kernel of a continuous homomorphism of étale fundamental groups is closed. -/
private theorem isClosed_ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap {Y Z : Scheme.{u}} [ConnectedSpace Y]
    [ConnectedSpace Z] (g : Y ⟶ Z) (y : GeometricPoint Y) :
    IsClosed (((etaleFundamentalGroupMap g y).toMonoidHom.ker) :
      Set (EtaleFundamentalGroup Y y)) := by
  have : T2Space (EtaleFundamentalGroup Z (y.map g)) := t2Space_etaleFundamentalGroup Z (y.map g)
  rw [MonoidHom.coe_ker]
  exact isClosed_singleton.preimage (etaleFundamentalGroupMap g y).continuous

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0BTD, the inclusion of subgroup (3) in subgroup (1).** Let `X` be an
integral scheme with function field `K`. The smallest closed normal subgroup of `π₁(Spec K)`
containing the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` for every point `x` of `X` is contained
in the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`.

For `X` normal the generating kernels are exactly the closed normal subgroups generated by the
images of the `π₁(Spec K_x^sh)`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_eq_normalClosure_topologicalClosure`
together with
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_eq`, so the subgroup on the left
is the third subgroup of the source and the one on the right is the first. -/
@[stacks 0BTD "the inclusion of subgroup (3) in subgroup (1), and only that inclusion: subgroup \
(1) is the kernel of π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X) rather than the subgroup fixing the maximal unramified \
subextension, so no Noetherian hypothesis is needed, and subgroup (3) is written with the \
kernels of π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x}) as generators; subgroup (2) is \
AlgebraicGeometry.inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup below"]
theorem normalClosure_iUnion_ker_topologicalClosure_le_ker [IsIntegral X]
    (p : GeometricPoint (Spec (X.residueField (genericPoint X)))) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ x : X,
          (((etaleFundamentalGroupMap (Spec.map (stalkToGenericResidueField X x))
            p).toMonoidHom.ker : Subgroup (EtaleFundamentalGroup
              (Spec (X.residueField (genericPoint X))) p)) : Set _))).topologicalClosure ≤
      (etaleFundamentalGroupMap (X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X))
        p).toMonoidHom.ker :=
  (Stacks.FundamentalGroup.normalClosure_iUnion_topologicalClosure_le_iff _
    (isClosed_ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap (X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X)) p)).mpr
    fun x => ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_le_ker X x p

/-! ### The generators of subgroup (3) -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0BTD, the generators of subgroup (3).** Let `X` be a normal integral
scheme with function field `K`, let `x` be a point of `X`, let `Ash` be a strict henselization of
`𝒪_{X,x}` and let `Ksh = K_x^sh` be its fraction field. The kernel of
`π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` is the smallest closed normal subgroup of `π₁(Spec K)`
containing the image of `π₁(Spec Ksh) = Gal(K^sep/K_x^sh)`.

This is the local exact sequence of Stacks Tag 0BSM applied to the local ring at `x`, whose
fraction field is the function field of `X` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isFractionRing_stalk_genericResidueField`. -/
@[stacks 0BTD "that each generator of subgroup (3) used here — the kernel of \
π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x}) — is the smallest closed normal subgroup containing the image of \
π₁(Spec K_x^sh) = Gal(K^sep/K_x^sh), which is how the source presents subgroup (3); this is Tag \
0BSM applied to the local rings of X"]
theorem ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_eq_normalClosure_topologicalClosure
    [IsIntegral X] [IsNormal X] (x : X) (κsep Ash Ksh : Type u)
    [CommRing Ash] [IsLocalRing Ash] [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash]
    [Field κsep] [Algebra (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) κsep]
    [IsSepClosure (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) κsep]
    [IsHenselization (X.presheaf.stalk x) κsep Ash]
    [Field Ksh] [Algebra Ash Ksh] [IsFractionRing Ash Ksh]
    [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ksh]
    [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh]
    [IsScalarTower (X.presheaf.stalk x) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh]
    [IsScalarTower (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash Ksh]
    (q : GeometricPoint (Spec (.of Ksh))) :
    (etaleFundamentalGroupMap (Spec.map (stalkToGenericResidueField X x))
        (q.map (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh))))).toMonoidHom.ker =
      (Subgroup.normalClosure (Set.range (etaleFundamentalGroupMap
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh))) q))).topologicalClosure := by
  have : IsIntegrallyClosed (X.presheaf.stalk x) := IsNormal.stalk_normal x
  exact (isExactSequence_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_fractionField_of_isHenselization
    (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash κsep (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh q).2.2

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0BTD, one generator of subgroup (3) lies in subgroup (1).** Let `X` be
a normal integral scheme with function field `K`, let `x` be a point of `X`, let `Ash` be a
strict henselization of `𝒪_{X,x}` and let `Ksh = K_x^sh` be its fraction field. The smallest
closed normal subgroup of `π₁(Spec K)` containing the image of
`π₁(Spec K_x^sh) = Gal(K^sep/K_x^sh)` is contained in the kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`.

This is the first paragraph of the source's proof, one point of `X` at a time: the image is
killed already by `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})`, by the local exact sequence of Stacks Tag
0BSM, and that homomorphism is a factor of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)`. -/
@[stacks 0BTD "that each generator Gal(K^sep/K_x^sh) of subgroup (3) generates a closed normal \
subgroup contained in subgroup (1), one point x of X at a time; subgroup (1) is the kernel of \
π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X), so no Noetherian hypothesis is needed; subgroup (2) is \
AlgebraicGeometry.inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup below"]
theorem normalClosure_range_topologicalClosure_le_ker
    [IsIntegral X] [IsNormal X] (x : X) (κsep Ash Ksh : Type u)
    [CommRing Ash] [IsLocalRing Ash] [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash]
    [Field κsep] [Algebra (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) κsep]
    [IsSepClosure (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) κsep]
    [IsHenselization (X.presheaf.stalk x) κsep Ash]
    [Field Ksh] [Algebra Ash Ksh] [IsFractionRing Ash Ksh]
    [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ksh]
    [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh]
    [IsScalarTower (X.presheaf.stalk x) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh]
    [IsScalarTower (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash Ksh]
    (q : GeometricPoint (Spec (.of Ksh))) :
    (Subgroup.normalClosure (Set.range (etaleFundamentalGroupMap
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
            (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh))) q))).topologicalClosure ≤
      (etaleFundamentalGroupMap (X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X))
        (q.map (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
          (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ksh))))).toMonoidHom.ker := by
  rw [← ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_eq_normalClosure_topologicalClosure X x κsep Ash Ksh q]
  exact ker_etaleFundamentalGroupMap_stalk_le_ker X x _

/-! ### The inclusion inside the absolute Galois group of the function field -/

section AbsoluteGaloisGroup

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X] (L Ω : Type u) [Field L] [Field Ω]
  [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L]
  [IsSepClosure (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L]
  [Algebra L Ω] [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ω]
  [IsScalarTower (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L Ω]
  [IsAlgClosed Ω] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ω]

/-- The kernel of the generic-point homomorphism `Gal(K^sep/K) → π₁(X)` is the preimage of the
kernel of `π₁(Spec K) → π₁(X)` under the identification of Stacks Tag 0BNE. -/
theorem ker_galoisToFundamentalGroup_eq_comap :
    (galoisToFundamentalGroup X L Ω).toMonoidHom.ker =
      Subgroup.comap (galoisEquivEtaleFundamentalGroup
          (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L Ω).toMonoidHom
        (etaleFundamentalGroupMap (X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X))
          (algebraicClosureGeometricPoint
            (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ω)).toMonoidHom.ker :=
  rfl

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0BTD, the inclusion of subgroup (3) in subgroup (1), inside
`Gal(K^sep/K)`.** Transporting along the identification `Gal(K^sep/K) = π₁(Spec K)` of Stacks Tag
0BNE, the smallest closed normal subgroup of `Gal(K^sep/K)` containing the kernel of
`Gal(K^sep/K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x})` for every point `x` of `X` is contained in the kernel of
`Gal(K^sep/K) → π₁(X)`. -/
@[stacks 0BTD "the inclusion of subgroup (3) in subgroup (1) read inside Gal(K^sep/K) through \
the identification of Tag 0BNE; subgroup (3) is written with the kernels of \
π₁(Spec K) → π₁(Spec 𝒪_{X,x}) as generators; subgroup (2) is \
AlgebraicGeometry.inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup below"]
theorem comap_normalClosure_iUnion_ker_le_ker_galoisToFundamentalGroup :
    Subgroup.comap (galoisEquivEtaleFundamentalGroup
        (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L Ω).toMonoidHom
      ((Subgroup.normalClosure (⋃ x : X,
          (((etaleFundamentalGroupMap (Spec.map (stalkToGenericResidueField X x))
            (algebraicClosureGeometricPoint
              (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ω)).toMonoidHom.ker : Subgroup
                (EtaleFundamentalGroup (Spec (X.residueField (genericPoint X)))
                  (algebraicClosureGeometricPoint
                    (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) Ω))) : Set _))).topologicalClosure) ≤
      (galoisToFundamentalGroup X L Ω).toMonoidHom.ker := by
  rw [ker_galoisToFundamentalGroup_eq_comap X L Ω]
  exact Subgroup.comap_mono (normalClosure_iUnion_ker_topologicalClosure_le_ker X _)

end AbsoluteGaloisGroup

/-! ### Subgroup (2): the inertia groups at the points of the normalization in `K^sep` -/

section Inertia

open scoped Pointwise

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsIntegral X] (E : Type u) [Field E]
  [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E]

/-- The sections on a nonempty open act on any extension `E` of the function field: restrict a
section to the generic point, pass to the residue field there, and extend scalars to `E`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def sectionsFunctionFieldExtAlgebra (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U] : Algebra Γ(X, U) E :=
  ((algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E).comp
    (X.germToFunctionField U ≫ X.residue (genericPoint X)).hom).toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] sectionsFunctionFieldExtAlgebra

/-- The function field sits between the sections on a nonempty open and any extension of it. -/
local instance isScalarTower_sectionsFunctionFieldExtAlgebra (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U] :
    IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E :=
  .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl

/-- A tower of extensions of the function field is a tower over the sections on any nonempty
open. -/
local instance isScalarTower_sections_tower (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U] (E' : Type u) [Field E']
    [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E'] [Algebra E E']
    [IsScalarTower (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E E'] :
    IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) E E' :=
  .of_algebraMap_eq fun x =>
    IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E E'
      (algebraMap Γ(X, U) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) x)

/-- **The residue field at the generic point is a fraction field of the sections on a nonempty
affine open.** This is the fraction-field property of the function field, read through the
residue isomorphism at the generic point. -/
theorem isFractionRing_sections_genericResidueField (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    [Nonempty U] : IsFractionRing Γ(X, U) (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) := by
  have := isIso_residue_genericPoint X
  have := functionField_isFractionRing_of_isAffineOpen X U hU
  let e : X.functionField ≃ₐ[Γ(X, U)] X.residueField (genericPoint X) :=
    { (asIso (X.residue (genericPoint X))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv with
      commutes' := fun _ => rfl }
  exact IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_algEquiv _ e

/-- The sections of a normal scheme on an affine open form an integrally closed domain. -/
theorem isIntegrallyClosed_sections [IsNormal X] (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    [Nonempty U] : IsIntegrallyClosed Γ(X, U) :=
  (AlgebraicGeometry.isNormal_iff_forall_affineOpen_normal X).mp inferInstance ⟨U, hU⟩
    inferInstance

/-- An algebraic extension of the function field is algebraic over the sections on a nonempty
affine open. -/
theorem isAlgebraic_sections (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) [Nonempty U]
    [Algebra.IsAlgebraic (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E] :
    Algebra.IsAlgebraic Γ(X, U) E := by
  let := isFractionRing_sections_genericResidueField X U hU
  exact (IsFractionRing.comap_isAlgebraic_iff (A := Γ(X, U))
    (K := X.residueField (genericPoint X)) (C := E)).mpr inferInstance

/-- An extension of the function field receives the sections on a nonempty open injectively. -/
theorem algebraMap_sections_injective (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U] :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap Γ(X, U) E) := by
  have hiso := isIso_residue_genericPoint X
  have h1 : Function.Injective (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E) :=
    (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E).injective
  have h2 : Function.Injective (X.residue (genericPoint X)) :=
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (X.residue (genericPoint X))).1
  have h3 := X.germToFunctionField_injective U
  intro a b hab
  exact h3 (h2 (h1 hab))

/-- **The integral closure of the sections on a nonempty affine open in an algebraic extension
of the function field has that extension as its fraction field.** -/
theorem isFractionRing_integralClosure_sections (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    [Nonempty U] [Algebra.IsAlgebraic (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E] :
    IsFractionRing (integralClosure Γ(X, U) E) E := by
  let := isFractionRing_sections_genericResidueField X U hU
  let := isAlgebraic_sections X E U hU
  exact integralClosure.isFractionRing_of_algebraic (A := Γ(X, U)) (L := E)
    fun _ hx => algebraMap_sections_injective X E U (hx.trans (map_zero _).symm)

variable [IsNormal X] (L : Type u) [Field L]
  [Algebra (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L]
  [IsSepClosure (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L]

/-- **The inertia groups of Stacks Tag 0BTD at the points of `X^sep` over an affine open.** The
points of the normalization `X^sep` of `X` in `K^sep` lying over a nonempty affine open `U` of
`X` are the primes of the integral closure `C` of `Γ(X, U)` in `K^sep`, and `Gal(K^sep/K)` acts
on `C`; the inertia group `I_y` at the point `y` given by a prime `r` of `C` is the subgroup of
elements acting as the identity on `C / r`. -/
def inertiaOverAffineOpen (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hne : Nonempty U) :
    Set Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X)) :=
  letI := hne
  letI := isFractionRing_sections_genericResidueField X U hU
  letI := isIntegrallyClosed_sections X U hU
  letI := isFractionRing_integralClosure_sections X L U hU
  letI := IsIntegralClosure.MulSemiringAction Γ(X, U)
    (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L (integralClosure Γ(X, U) L)
  {σ | ∃ r : Ideal (integralClosure Γ(X, U) L), r.IsPrime ∧
    σ ∈ r.inertia Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X))}

/-- **The generators of subgroup (2) of Stacks Tag 0BTD.** The union of the inertia groups `I_y`
over all points `y` of `X^sep`: every such point lies over some nonempty affine open of `X`. -/
def inertiaGenerators : Set Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X)) :=
  ⋃ (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hne : Nonempty U),
    inertiaOverAffineOpen X L U hU hne

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- The inertia groups at the points of `X^sep` over a nonempty affine open `U` are contained in
`inertiaGenerators X L`. -/
theorem inertiaOverAffineOpen_subset_inertiaGenerators (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hne : Nonempty U) :
    inertiaOverAffineOpen X L U hU hne ⊆ inertiaGenerators X L :=
  Set.subset_iUnion_of_subset U <| Set.subset_iUnion_of_subset hU <|
    Set.subset_iUnion (fun hne => inertiaOverAffineOpen X L U hU hne) hne

/-- **Subgroup (2) of Stacks Tag 0BTD.** The smallest closed normal subgroup of
`Gal(K^sep/K) = π₁(Spec K)` containing the inertia group `I_y` for every point `y` of the
normalization `X^sep` of `X` in `K^sep`. -/
@[stacks 0BTD "subgroup (2): the smallest closed normal subgroup of Gal(K^sep/K) containing \
the inertia group I_y for every point y of the normalization X^sep of X in K^sep, with the \
points of X^sep over a nonempty affine open U of X presented as the primes of the integral \
closure of Γ(X, U) in K^sep"]
def inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup : Subgroup Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X)) :=
  (Subgroup.normalClosure (inertiaGenerators X L)).topologicalClosure

/-- `inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L` is a normal subgroup. -/
instance : (inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L).Normal :=
  Subgroup.is_normal_topologicalClosure _

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- `inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L` is closed in `Gal(K^sep/K)`. -/
theorem isClosed_inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup :
    IsClosed ((inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L : Subgroup _) :
      Set Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X))) :=
  Subgroup.isClosed_topologicalClosure _

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- Every inertia group `I_y` is contained in `inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L`. -/
theorem inertiaGenerators_subset_inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup :
    inertiaGenerators X L ⊆
      ((inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L : Subgroup _) :
        Set Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X))) :=
  Stacks.FundamentalGroup.subset_normalClosure_topologicalClosure _

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- Subgroup (2) is contained in a closed normal subgroup exactly when every inertia group is. -/
theorem inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup_le_iff
    {N : Subgroup Gal(L/X.residueField (genericPoint X))} [N.Normal]
    (hN : IsClosed (N : Set Gal(L/X.residueField (genericPoint X)))) :
    inertiaClosedNormalSubgroup X L ≤ N ↔
      inertiaGenerators X L ⊆ (N : Set Gal(L / X.residueField (genericPoint X))) :=
  Stacks.FundamentalGroup.normalClosure_topologicalClosure_le_iff hN

/-! #### The reverse inclusion `(1) ⊆ (2)` -/

/-- The function field acts on an extension of the residue field at the generic point through
the residue map there; for an integral scheme that map is an isomorphism, so this presents the
same extension over the function field. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def functionFieldExtAlgebra : Algebra X.functionField E :=
  ((algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E).comp
    (X.residue (genericPoint X)).hom).toAlgebra

attribute [local instance] functionFieldExtAlgebra

/-- The function field, the residue field at the generic point and `E` form a scalar tower. -/
local instance isScalarTower_functionFieldExtAlgebra :
    IsScalarTower X.functionField (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E :=
  .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl

/-- The sections over a nonempty open `U`, the function field and `E` form a scalar tower. -/
local instance isScalarTower_sections_functionField (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U] :
    IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) X.functionField E :=
  .of_algebraMap_eq' rfl

/-- The inclusion of an extension of the function field into a larger one carries the integral
closure of the sections on an open into the integral closure there. -/
def integralClosureInclusion (U : X.Opens) [Nonempty U]
    (F : IntermediateField (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L) :
    integralClosure Γ(X, U) F →+* integralClosure Γ(X, U) L where
  toFun b := ⟨algebraMap F L b.1,
    b.2.map (IsScalarTower.toAlgHom Γ(X, U) (F : Type u) L)⟩
  map_one' := Subtype.ext (map_one _)
  map_mul' _ _ := Subtype.ext (map_mul _ _ _)
  map_zero' := Subtype.ext (map_zero _)
  map_add' _ _ := Subtype.ext (map_add _ _ _)

/-- The residue map at the generic point of an integral scheme, as an isomorphism of the function
field with the residue field there. -/
@[sga "3 VIB 10.10" "identification O_{X"]
def functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField :
    X.functionField ≃+* X.residueField (genericPoint X) :=
  have := isIso_residue_genericPoint X
  (asIso (X.residue (genericPoint X))).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- `functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField X` is the residue map at the generic point. -/
theorem functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField_apply (a : X.functionField) :
    functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField X a = X.residue (genericPoint X) a := rfl

/-- The residue field at the generic point is finite-dimensional over the function field: the two
are isomorphic. -/
local instance finiteDimensional_functionField_genericResidueField :
    FiniteDimensional X.functionField (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) :=
  Module.Finite.of_surjective
    (Algebra.linearMap X.functionField (X.residueField (genericPoint X)))
    (functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField X).surjective

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- A finite extension of the residue field at the generic point is finite over the function
field. -/
theorem finiteDimensional_functionField
    [FiniteDimensional (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E] :
    FiniteDimensional X.functionField E :=
  .trans X.functionField (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- A Galois extension of the residue field at the generic point is Galois over the function
field. -/
theorem isGalois_functionField [IsGalois (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E] :
    IsGalois X.functionField E :=
  IsGalois.of_equiv_equiv (F := X.residueField (genericPoint X)) (E := E)
    (f := (functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField X).symm) (g := RingEquiv.refl E)
    (by
      ext a
      exact congrArg (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E)
        ((functionFieldEquivGenericResidueField X).apply_symm_apply a))

omit [IsNormal X] in
/-- The generic-point morphism of an extension of the function field, written through the
function field rather than through the residue field at the generic point. -/
theorem specMap_algebraMap_fromSpecResidueField_eq :
    Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) E)) ≫
        X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap X.functionField E)) ≫
        X.fromSpecStalk (genericPoint X) := by
  rw [Scheme.fromSpecResidueField, ← Spec.map_comp_assoc]
  rfl

/-- **Stacks Tag 0BTD, the inertia criterion for unramifiedness.** Let `X` be a normal integral
scheme with function field `K` and let `F` be a finite Galois subextension of `K^sep / K` whose
fixing subgroup contains every inertia group `I_y` for `y` a point of `X^sep` — equivalently,
with `F` inside the fixed field of subgroup (2). Then the normalization of `X` in `F` is finite
étale over `X`, that is, `X` is unramified in `F`.

This is the second paragraph of the source's proof. The points of `X^sep` over a nonempty affine
open `U` of `X` are the primes of the integral closure `C` of `Γ(X, U)` in `K^sep`, and the
points of the normalization of `X` in `F` over `U` are the primes of the integral closure `B` of
`Γ(X, U)` in `F`. Every prime of `B` is the contraction of a prime of `C`, and restriction
carries the inertia group at a prime of `C` onto the inertia group at its contraction, which is
Stacks Tag 0BSX. The hypothesis makes every element of the former restrict to the identity, so
all the latter are trivial and the normalization is unramified by Stacks Tag 0BTF. -/
@[stacks 0BTD "the second paragraph of the proof: triviality of the inertia groups I_y on a \
finite Galois subextension F of K^sep/K makes X unramified in F",
  sga "1 V 2.2" "(ii)",
  sga "1 V 2.3" "special case"]
theorem isFinite_etale_fromNormalization_of_inertiaGenerators_subset
    (F : IntermediateField (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) L)
    [FiniteDimensional (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) F]
    [IsGalois (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) F]
    (hF : inertiaGenerators X L ⊆
      (F.fixingSubgroup : Set Gal(L/X.residueField (genericPoint X)))) :
    let f : Spec (.of (F : Type u)) ⟶ X :=
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
        (algebraMap (X.residueField (genericPoint X)) (F : Type u))) ≫
        X.fromSpecResidueField (genericPoint X)
    IsFinite f.fromNormalization ∧ Etale f.fromNormalization := by
  let := finiteDimensional_functionField X (F : Type u)
  let := isGalois_functionField X (F : Type u)
  intro f
  have hi : f = Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap X.functionField (F : Type u))) ≫
      X.fromSpecStalk (genericPoint X) :=
    specMap_algebraMap_fromSpecResidueField_eq X (F : Type u)
  have hunram : Unramified f.fromNormalization := by
    refine (normalization_unramified_iff_trivialInertia X (F : Type u) f hi).mpr ?_
    intro U hU hne q hq σ hσ
    let := hne
    let := isFractionRing_sections_genericResidueField X U hU
    let := isIntegrallyClosed_sections X U hU
    let := functionField_isFractionRing_of_isAffineOpen X U hU
    let := isFractionRing_integralClosure_sections X L U hU
    let := isFractionRing_integralClosure_sections X (F : Type u) U hU
    let algBC : Algebra (integralClosure Γ(X, U) (F : Type u)) (integralClosure Γ(X, U) L) :=
      (integralClosureInclusion X L U F).toAlgebra
    let algBL : Algebra (integralClosure Γ(X, U) (F : Type u)) L :=
      ((algebraMap (F : Type u) L).comp
        (algebraMap (integralClosure Γ(X, U) (F : Type u)) (F : Type u))).toAlgebra
    have hinj : Function.Injective
        (algebraMap (integralClosure Γ(X, U) (F : Type u)) (integralClosure Γ(X, U) L)) := by
      intro x y hxy
      refine Subtype.ext ((algebraMap (F : Type u) L).injective ?_)
      exact congrArg (fun z : integralClosure Γ(X, U) L => (z : L)) hxy
    let twrBCL : IsScalarTower (integralClosure Γ(X, U) (F : Type u))
        (integralClosure Γ(X, U) L) L := .of_algebraMap_eq fun _ => rfl
    let twrABC : IsScalarTower Γ(X, U) (integralClosure Γ(X, U) (F : Type u))
